Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:11:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Promotion: a re-ingested entry keeps its licence and its kept
 table transcription

The promotion builds an entry's JSON-LD nodes from the staged tree. On
a re-ingest that tree lacks what no rung writes: the entry's
licence.json, and a table transcription the table arm kept rather than
draft over. So a re-ingested entry's manifest lost its licence, and its
table blocks named drafts it did not keep (re-ingest pilot,
2026-11-15: two handbooks without their CC BY-NC-SA licence; 10665-75211
with 81 draft-table blocks over its 27 transcribed tables).

carryAuthored copies them from the filed entry into staging when staging
lacks them, before the nodes are built; a staged file is never replaced.
Summaries and errata stay out: they name blocks, and the gate would judge
them against a re-split entry's new ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPfb62Puokdy7SvkiNR
